# Never run SQL on Sim Bleepy

This repo is Sim Bleepy. The user runs all SQL. You do not.

Do **not**:

- `supabase db query`, `supabase db push`, `supabase migration up`, or `--linked` SQL
- `exec_sql` / any RPC that executes SQL
- `psql`, dashboard API, or a script whose job is to apply SQL
- Service-role calls that create/alter tables or run raw SQL
- Apply a migration because “the feature needs it”

Do:

- Write the `.sql` file in the repo if needed
- Tell the user the file path and the exact SQL to paste (Supabase SQL editor)
- Wait until they say it has been run before depending on new tables/columns
- If SQL is required and has not been run, say so — do not ship a schema workaround

Bleepy App handoff docs are write-ups only. Never run SQL there either from this repo.
